WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.710
Hi, I'm Kedge!

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:06.712
A decision model reads a photo and answers typed questions about it.

00:00:06.712 --> 00:00:10.380
This one reads the photo once, however many questions you ask.

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:14.860
The idea: the state stops looking at the question.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.374
So it is the same for every question, and is computed once.

00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:25.742
In d3, the state reads the question, so every question pays

00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:27.003
for the photo again.

00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:29.951
In d3-turbo, the state reads only itself.

00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:31.757
The photo is read once.

00:00:33.758 --> 00:00:37.563
First, the photo and the text run through all sixty-four layers, once.

00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:41.677
The runtime keeps the attention keys and values, and the final state

00:00:41.677 --> 00:00:42.909
of each linear scan.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:46.345
Then the short question blocks run on top, each reading the

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:47.442
cached state and itself.

00:00:47.862 --> 00:00:51.542
A readout over answer codes gives every option a probability.

00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:53.014
No text is generated.

00:00:54.842 --> 00:00:59.818
At two hundred fifty-five questions, the vendor times thirty-three seconds for the

00:00:59.818 --> 00:01:02.721
smaller d3-flash, and about two for d3-turbo.

00:01:04.275 --> 00:01:06.283
Box questions reuse the same readout.

00:01:07.142 --> 00:01:10.566
Each edge is a distribution over one hundred twenty-eight steps.

00:01:10.986 --> 00:01:12.068
The edge is its mean.

00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:17.696
Draw five hundred twelve boxes, and count how many overlap the answer.

00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:20.376
A table turns that share into the confidence.

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:24.415
Four questions, four boxes, each with a confidence.

00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:26.368
The camera gets low confidence.

00:01:26.368 --> 00:01:28.514
That is the confidence doing its job.

00:01:30.175 --> 00:01:33.238
Number one on both boards was the team's own estimate.

00:01:33.238 --> 00:01:36.607
On the official text board it is tenth, tied with d3.

00:01:38.225 --> 00:01:40.894
Keep the state from reading the question, and you are allowed

00:01:40.894 --> 00:01:41.865
to read it once.

00:01:46.275 --> 00:01:50.357
Read once, cached, and the same accuracy as d3, with far less waiting.

00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:52.914
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.914 --> 00:01:53.497
I'm Kedge.

00:01:53.497 --> 00:01:53.788
Bye!
